Manga Panels (黑白漫画分格) — "KOMA ONE: Thirty Frames a Second" (library demo)
Every asset in the film, with its source and licence.

BRAND, PRODUCT, CHARACTER
- KOMA, the KOMA ONE pocket camera and the street photographer are fictional, made for this demo.
  "KOMA" (コマ) is the Japanese word for a manga panel and a film frame.
- The camera is an original design in the general design language of rangefinder-style retro cameras
  (silver top and bottom plates, leatherette, short prime lens, viewfinder window, knurled dials).
  It copies no real brand or model and carries no logo, badge, lettering or numbers.

IMAGES (Codex image generation · Codex 生图)
- These images belong to this demo only. A film in this style generates its own images for its own topic;
  the demo's character, camera and city are not for reuse, recolouring or editing into another film.
- All 15 drawings were generated with Codex image generation (OpenAI image generation through the Codex CLI,
  core/image/gen_image.py) from the prompts in prompts/, each with the style suffix in
  tools/style_suffix.txt. Re-printed as screentone by tools/prep.py. No photo, existing artwork, character or
  logo was used as a reference; the only references are images generated for this film.
- The photographer: character reference char_shoot (no ref), then every pose with --ref to it (tools/gen_all.sh).
- The camera: product reference prod_hero; the other ten images that show the camera are edits in edit mode
  (the first drawing of the same pose + prod_hero, "replace only the camera"; tools/gen_camswap.sh,
  prompts/prod_hero_redesign.txt, prompts/_camswap*.txt).
- Backgrounds and inserts without the camera: bg_city, pigeons, feet, crowd (prompts/*.txt).

